  "summary": "Chandler, AZ city council tabled renewal of its Flock Safety ALPR contract after residents objected that cameras were concentrated in predominantly Hispanic neighborhoods, including one pointed at Galveston Elementary School. That camera was physically removed during the meeting, and a councilmember unsuccessfully pushed to deactivate all 40 cameras pending a July decision.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "After council members and residents clashed Thursday night, the city's contract renewal with Flock Safety was tabled.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "That's simply from the public pressure, and we can greatly increase that public pressure as much as we need to, in order to get Flock out of Chandler",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "Council member OD Harris pushed to have all 40 cameras turned off until a final decision is made in July.",
      "paragraph_idx": 22
    }
  ],
